course: dictionary
lesson: 4393
title: Everyday words: hairbrush
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are everyday words that you use without thinking. A hairbrush is one of them. You can work out its meaning from its two parts: hair and brush. A brush is a tool with bristles, so a hairbrush is a brush for your hair.
explain: Read «Head lice and germs can spread through shared helmets, hats and hairbrushes.» The clue is the word shared. If people share something, they all use it, so a hairbrush is something that can pass from person to person. The sentence warns that sharing can spread germs.
explain: Now read «He parted his hair in the middle, and plastered it down very straight and sleek with water from his hairbrush, and went quietly down the stairs.» The hairbrush is the tool he used to make his hair smooth and tidy. Check it by swapping in your meaning: "with water from his brush for smooth tidy hair" still makes sense.
fact: A hairbrush is a brush with a handle, used to make your hair smooth and tidy.
fact: Hairbrush is a noun, and its plural is hairbrushes.
fact: A round hairbrush is a hairbrush with a round shape.
fact: You brush your hair with a hairbrush, often in the morning.
fact: Keep your own hairbrush and do not share it, because sharing can spread head lice.
exercise: «Head lice and germs can spread through shared helmets, hats and hairbrushes.» What is a hairbrush used for? | *To make your hair smooth and tidy | To clean the floor | To hold up a tent | To keep your feet warm
exercise: Why should you not share your hairbrush with a friend? | Because it is made of gold | *Because head lice and germs can spread through it | Because it is too big to carry | Because hairbrushes only work for grown-ups
exercise: Find and copy the plural form of hairbrush from «Head lice and germs can spread through shared helmets, hats and hairbrushes.» | *hairbrushes | shared | hairbrush | hair
test: In «He parted his hair in the middle, and plastered it down very straight and sleek with water from his hairbrush», what did he use the hairbrush for? | To play a tune | To wash the dog | *To make his hair smooth and sleek | To paint the wall
test: Which word in «a round hairbrush» tells you about its shape? | *round | brush | a | hair
exam: Ella says, «I'll use my friend's hairbrush so I don't need mine.» Why is this a bad idea? | *It can spread head lice and germs | It only works when it is wet | It is too heavy to lift | Hairbrushes are only for pets
